WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.926
A subscriber records an experiment-completed event
and then sends a researcher a notification.

00:00:05.926 --> 00:00:12.168
If it crashes after sending but before recording
progress, a retry can send the notification again.

00:00:12.168 --> 00:00:18.472
Repeated delivery and repeated business effects are
different issues: a stable event identifier lets

00:00:18.472 --> 00:00:24.588
the handler recognize a prior effect only when the
relevant state is recorded with an appropriate

00:00:24.588 --> 00:00:25.659
consistency rule.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:30.080
Simply labelling the handler idempotent does not
establish that rule.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.381
Now deliver result version three before version two.

00:00:33.381 --> 00:00:38.967
Duplicate detection alone cannot prevent an old
version from overwriting a newer result.

00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:43.919
Define ordering per experiment or reject obsolete
updates using their version.

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:50.140
When a malformed event repeatedly fails, bound
retries and retain enough information for diagnosis

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:51.536
and controlled replay.

00:00:51.536 --> 00:00:57.508
Monitor subscription age as well as message counts
so a small set of stuck events is visible.

00:00:57.508 --> 00:01:03.672
These decisions belong to the consumer contract and
broker configuration; a distributed delivery

00:01:03.672 --> 00:01:10.029
system does not offer one universal ordering or
exactly-once guarantee for every downstream effect.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:14.828
The robotics example organizes computation into
nodes with typed messages.

00:01:14.828 --> 00:01:21.109
Topics carry streams such as sensor readings,
services provide request-and-response interactions,

00:01:21.109 --> 00:01:25.383
and actions support longer goals with progress and a
final result.

00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:31.534
These interfaces let sensing, planning, control and
visualization evolve separately while still

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:38.009
communicating through explicit data contracts suited
to their interaction patterns and timing needs.
